CreaSDK is the assembly kit for creative monetization: payments, subscriptions, content distribution, and community operations, packaged as independent modules.

# Assemble, don't adopt

Most platforms ask a creator to move everything onto their rails. CreaSDK asks what you already have. Each module has a narrow interface and communicates over gRPC, so a team can adopt payments alone, or add subscriptions later without rewriting the product.

# One interface over many rails

The payments module abstracts Stripe, Alipay, and WeChat Pay behind a single transaction API and callback model. The subscription module handles one-time purchases, recurring plans, usage-based billing, and tiered pricing. The goal is not to hide the payment providers — it is to keep settlement logic out of every product surface.

# Distribution with control

The content module provides encryption, entitlement checks, and a distribution pipeline that can target by region, tier, or access level. Creators can put paid content behind an API call instead of building a DRM system from scratch. The community module adds discussion, feedback collection, and user behavior analysis without another vendor.

# Beta, in public

CreaSDK is in beta with 412 GitHub stars. The next milestone is multi-language SDKs — TypeScript, Python, and Rust — so the same primitives are available to every stack.
